s=\"noborder txt-black\">Status</td></tr><tr><td class=\"txt-black bg-blue\">You</td><td class=\"txt-muted\">0 sec</td><td><span class=\"tst-status status-unat\">Unattempted</span></td></tr><tr><td class=\"txt-black bg-blue\">Topper</td><td class=\"txt-muted\">18 sec</td><td><span class=\"tst-status status-correct\">Correct</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><span class=\"eqt\"><p>The question contains pairs of words that are related to each other in a certain way. Three of the following four word pairs are alike as these have the same relationship and thus form a group. Which word pair is the one that DOES NOT belong to that group? </p><p>(The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters / number of consonants/vowels in the word.)</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2319;&#2325; &#2332;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367; &#2311;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2357;&#2361; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;? </p><p>(&#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; / &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; / &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;)</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Bone - orthopaedic</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2337;&#2381;&#2337;&#2368; - &#2310;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2379;&#2346;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2325;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Uterus - urologist</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2366;&#2358;&#2351; - &#2350;&#2370;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2352;&#2379;&#2327; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Stomach - gastroenterologist</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2375;&#2335; - &#2327;&#2376;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2319;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2352;&#2379;&#2354;&#2377;&#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Eye - ophthalmologist</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; - &#2344;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2352;&#2379;&#2327; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The first word in each pair represents a body part, and the second word represents a medical specialist associated with that body part. We need to check if the relationships are accurate.</p><p><b>Option 1: Bone  -  orthopaedic</b></p><p>&#183; Orthopaedic specialists deal with disorders related to bones.</p><p>&#183; <b>Correct relationship.</b></p><p><b>Option 2: Uterus  -  urologist</b></p><p>&#183; Urologists specialize in the urinary system, including kidneys, bladder, and urethra.</p><p>&#183; However, the uterus is not primarily treated by a urologist. Specialists for the uterus are gynecologists.</p><p>&#183; <b>Incorrect relationship.</b></p><p><b>Option 3: Stomach  -  gastroenterologist</b></p><p>&#183; Gastroenterologists specialize in the digestive system, including the stomach.</p><p>&#183; <b>Correct relationship.</b></p><p><b>Option 4: Eye  -  ophthalmologist</b></p><p>&#183; Ophthalmologists specialize in eye disorders and diseases.</p><p>&#183; <b>Correct relationship.</b></p><p><b>Final Answer:</b></p><p>The word pair that does not belong to the group is option (b) Uterus-urologist</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}